^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §11b: custom data descriptor read. A class attribute
bound to a descriptor-class instance (one defining __get__) is typed as
that class, and the attribute read dispatches __get__ (resolved via the
MRO) rather than returning the stored value. Stateful descriptors whose
__get__ reads self are over-approximated (the class-object storage is
not yet constructed), and descriptor __set__ on write is not yet
modeled.
